 R←Test_009(debugFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;key;ps;query;lines;iconUri;i
⍝ Exercise the whole chain with `toast.ps1` doing its job. Whether a toast really appeared on
⍝ the screen is something only a human can tell, so this test asks.
⍝ The icon needs no human: `toast.ps1` registers it, so it can be read back.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If batchFlag
     R←T._NoBatchTest ⋄ →0
 :ElseIf 'Win'≢3↑⊃# ⎕WG'APLVersion'
     R←T._WindowsOnly ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=##.WindowsToast.⎕NC'TatinVars'   ⍝ `tatinVars` in the Cider config puts it where a loaded package has it

 key←'HKCU:\SOFTWARE\Classes\AppUserModelId\Dyalog.APL.CommTools'   ⍝ The app ID `toast.ps1` registers
 ps←'powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command '
 query←ps,'"(Get-ItemProperty -LiteralPath ''',key,''' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).IconUri"'
 ⍝ Away with whatever an earlier run registered, so the check below cannot pass on a leftover
 {}⎕CMD ps,'"Remove-ItemProperty -LiteralPath ''',key,''' -Name IconUri -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue"'

 →T.GoToTidyUp~1 CommTools.YesOrNo'Test_009@Test_009: can you see this question in a toast?'

 ⍝ The toast is fired and forgotten: `Notify` returned after 17 ms while `toast.ps1` took another
 ⍝ 795 ms to reach the registry, so the value is waited for rather than read just once.
 lines←⍬
 :For i :In ⍳25
     lines←⎕CMD query
     :If 0<≢lines
         :Leave
     :EndIf
     ⎕DL 0.2
 :EndFor
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0=≢lines                          ⍝ Five seconds, and nothing was registered at all
 iconUri←⊃lines
 →T.GoToTidyUp'.png'≢¯4↑iconUri                  ⍝ Windows shows no icon when this names an `.exe`
 →T.GoToTidyUp~⎕NEXISTS iconUri

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
⍝Done
